Announcing the 3.5.2 release of UnNetHack.

Unfortunately this release breaks bones and save file compatibility
with 3.5.1.

Source code and Win32 tty download:
http://sourceforge.net/projects/unnethack/files/

Trac project page:
http://apps.sf.net/trac/unnethack/



Changelog of the most important changes (complete list is on the
project page):

Added Patches:
 Added potions of blood and vampire blood (from Slash'Em)
 Bag of Tricks Enhancement Patch (by Nephi)
 Blood-sucking and biting Vampire patch (from Slash'Em)
 Breaking a camera may release a picture painting demon (by L)
 Cancellation patch (by Malcolm Ryan)
 Color Alchemy (by Nephi)
 Free Fortune Cookie (by Nephi)
 Monk specific greeting and goodbye (by Haakon Studebaker)
 Oily corpses patch (by L)
 qwertz_layout (by Stanislav Traykov)
 While Helpless (by Pasi Kallinen)

Changes to monsters:
 Color of floating eyes changed to bright green
 Renamed dragons and their scales

Changes to objects:
 Feedback for teleporting Amulet of Yendor when player is blind
 Feedback from scrolls of earth in end game
 Less guarranted stuff in Vlad's tower
 Trollsbane: grants hungerless regeneration
 Vorpal Blade: +1d8 special damage
 Wishing for specific dragon armor only works correctly when armor is known

Misc:
 Bones: Remove objects randomly from dead player's inventory
 Interrupt a multi turn action if hit points or magical energy is restored
 Livelog: Report killing of former player in bones
 Livelog: Report killing of unique monsters
 Livelog: Report successful shopliftings
 Prevent crash when rn2 <= 0 is called
 Riders: show real name if rider is next to player or can be seen
 Vibrating square: Messages when player is near

Fixes:
 Bear trap acting like sleeping gas trap for some monsters
 Correct color for black on Windows console
 Don't split a stack of wielded, cursed weapons
 Fix: catching thrown objects didn't clear their was_thrown-bit
 Fix number of random heck levels
 Fix transformation of corpses into giant ant corpses on pickup
 Fix transformation of tins into giant ant tins on pickup
 Prevent the player from being enclosed by stone when coming from the valley
 Upstairs room for minetown-1 was unplacable

Fixes of official bugs:
 C343-55  "Ulch" messages have inconsistent capitalization.
 C343-116 Grammar error in messages related to choking on gold.
 C343-136 A samurai quest guardian message uses "ninja" where "ronin" is intended. 
 C343-211 Engraving under water gives a poorly worded message.
 C343-231 Time is distorted while sinking into lava.


